css='''@font-face{font-family:Schibsted;src:url('../../fonts/SchibstedGrotesk-Regular.ttf')}@font-face{font-family:Schibsted;src:url('../../fonts/SchibstedGrotesk-Medium.ttf');font-weight:500}*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;background:#f1f1ef;color:#252923;font:17px/1.65 Schibsted,system-ui,sans-serif}main,nav,footer{max-width:1120px;margin:auto;padding:0 32px}nav{padding-top:28px;padding-bottom:24px;border-bottom:1px solid #cbd0c3;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:24px}.brand{font-size:28px;letter-spacing:-1px;font-weight:500;text-decoration:none}.brand span{color:#637e30}.small{font-size:13px;color:#566347}a{color:inherit;text-underline-offset:4px}a:focus-visible,summary:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #36552d;outline-offset:5px}header{padding:58px 0 44px}.eyebrow{font-size:13px;color:#566347}h1{font-size:clamp(36px,5vw,64px);line-height:1.12;letter-spacing:-.045em;font-weight:500;max-width:850px;margin:20px 0 24px}h2{font-size:30px;font-weight:500;line-height:1.3;letter-spacing:-.03em;margin:0 0 24px}h3{font-size:19px;font-weight:500}.lead{font-size:21px;color:#4d5c43;max-width:810px}.status{padding:20px 24px;background:#e5edd4;border-left:4px solid #6d843e;margin-top:30px}.status strong{display:block}section{padding:44px 0;border-top:1px solid #cbd0c3}p{margin:0 0 18px}li{margin:10px 0}strong{font-weight:500}.table-wrap{overflow-x:auto}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:15px}td,th{text-align:left;vertical-align:top;padding:18px 12px;border-bottom:1px solid #cbd0c3}th{font-weight:500}th:first-child{padding-left:0;min-width:190px}td:last-child{white-space:nowrap;color:#4d5c43}details{border-top:1px solid #cbd0c3;padding:20px 0}summary{font-weight:500;font-size:18px;cursor:pointer}details p{margin-top:16px}details li{font-size:15px}.rule-list{max-width:860px}.debate{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:28px}.debate p{font-size:15px}footer{padding-top:28px;padding-bottom:40px;border-top:1px solid #cbd0c3;font-size:13px;color:#566347}.button{display:inline-block;background:#36552d;color:#fff;padding:12px 18px;border-radius:4px;text-decoration:none;margin:10px 18px 0 0}code{overflow-wrap:anywhere;font-size:12px}@media(max-width:650px){main,nav,footer{padding-left:20px;padding-right:20px}nav .small{max-width:155px;text-align:right}header{padding-top:36px}h1{font-size:39px}.lead{font-size:18px}.status{padding:16px}.debate{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:12px}table{font-size:14px}th:first-child{min-width:135px}.table-wrap{margin:0 -4px}header>.button{display:table;margin-bottom:16px}header>.button+a{display:table}td,th{padding:14px 8px}section{padding:36px 0}}'''
html=f'''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>heyNag — the team’s quality plan</title><style>{css}</style></head><body><nav><a class="brand" href="../../animation-v5/index.html">heyNag<span>.</span></a><span class="small">18 specialists · GPT-6 Astra<br>Ultra reasoning · 7 November 2026</span></nav><main><header><p class="eyebrow">EXPANDED TEAM REVIEW</p><h1>A more memorable<br>little moth.</h1><p class="lead">Preserve the little moth. Give it more distinctly Nag-like acting, more deliberate drawing, and evidence that supports every quality judgment.</p><div class="status"><strong>18 of 18 endorse the same plan.</strong>Nine pairs discussed the work. All eighteen registered individual agreement with named evidence limits. No substantive objection remains to this plan. Current artwork and scores have not been upgraded by this decision.</div><a class="button" href="#work">See the agreed work</a><a href="#debates">See what the panel challenged</a></header>
<section id="work"><h2>What each discipline needs to see.</h2><p>These are the concrete improvements and proof each pair will look for when reconsidering its score.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Discipline</th><th>Quality target</th><th>Plan vote</th></tr></thead><tbody>{''.join(rows)}</tbody></table></div></section>
<section id="debates"><h2>Agreement followed real challenges.</h2><div class="debate"><div><h3>Explore before something breaks.</h3><p>Performance B objected to requiring a demonstrated failure before trying an alternative. The shared plan resolves it: reversible artistic exploration is welcome; adoption needs a named benefit.</p></div><div><h3>A creature’s name is not the brand goal.</h3><p>The identity and audience pairs separated “does this look like a moth?” from “do people associate it with Nag?” A sprout-like reading alone does not justify sacrificing the useful head avatar.</p></div><div><h3>Contact can carry feeling.</h3><p>The drawing and rigging pairs challenged automatic mitten separation. Grateful hands may stay joined; the question is whether the intended gesture reads.</p></div><div><h3>A recall test can rehearse the answer.</h3><p>The audience pair corrected the proposed delayed-memory protocol. An immediate question changes later recall; the study must report that sequence or reserve a separate first-probe group.</p></div></div></section>
<section><h2>The implementation brief.</h2><p>Start with the known reading-key issue and the signature acting study. Develop tightly scoped visual and timing alternatives alongside the unchanged control.</p>{''.join(packages)}<p class="small">Every reviewer voted on the exact same <a href="team-proposal-v1.json">proposal</a>. <a href="consensus.json">Consensus record</a><br><code>{digest}</code></p></section>
<section><h2>How scores will remain honest.</h2><ol class="rule-list"><li>State which artifact, use size and quality dimension the score covers.</li><li>Name the evidence actually inspected, strengths, deductions and confidence.</li><li>Explain what observable improvement could change the judgment.</li><li>Keep each reviewer’s number. Agreement on the plan does not require identical ratings.</li><li>Use “not yet scored” when relevant evidence is missing. A source or still review cannot certify felt motion timing.</li><li>Keep Nag’s preference, expert craft judgments and actual audience findings separate.</li></ol><p>The current independent records retain scoped judgments of 8 for static identity craft, 8.4 for static material/theme quality, and 7.5 for static perceptual readiness. Other reviewers withheld numbers. These assess different scopes and should not be averaged into a product score. The 8.4 is a subjective judgment, not measurement precision.</p><p><a href="score-policy.json">Read the scoring policy</a></p></section>
<section><h2>All eighteen positions, preserved.</h2><p>Two complementary reviewers per discipline. The original reviews, objections, partner responses and final votes remain available for future engineering and website work.</p>{''.join(details)}</section>
<section><h2>What happens next.</h2><p>This completes the expanded panel’s review and agreement on the next work. The current source remains unchanged. The plan’s acting, visual and interaction improvements still need implementation and fresh review before any higher score can be earned.</p><p>No human recognition, attachment or delayed-recall results exist yet. Optional sound, new worlds and website deployment remain later work.</p><p><a href="../../team.json">Standing roster</a> · <a href="../../../AGENTS.md">Engineering review instructions</a> · <a href="../../animation-v5/index.html">Current motion studio</a> · <a href="../2026-11-07-refinement/index.html">Previous refinement</a></p></section></main><footer>heyNag · Nag / Nagarjuna Boddu · Quality first<br>Model settings were explicit for all eighteen agents. Runtime availability may change; roles and review history remain in the repository.</footer></body></html>'''
